What is a Framework?

A framework is a pre-built software platform that provides ready-made tools, libraries, rules, and components to help developers build applications faster and more efficiently.

Instead of writing everything from scratch, developers use a framework as a foundation.

Simple Analogy

Imagine building a house.

🧱 Without a framework: You make every brick, door, and window yourself.
🏠 With a framework: The foundation, walls, and structure are already prepared. You just customize and complete the house.

The same idea applies to software development.

